      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah, I believe the runner should do something like:\n\n```\nboolean initialA2dpSourceValue \u003d getprop(bluetooth.profile.a2dp.source.enabled)\nsetprop(bluetooth.profile.a2dp.source.enabled, false)\n\nrun test\n\nsetprop(bluetooth.profile.a2dp.source.enabled, initialA2dpSourceValue)\n```\n\n(but while using your class wrapper that does that nicely for all property)",
